From 4f2c51f78d3148600bc8587bb57aeebe435658df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:49:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/17] feat(mcp): de-duplicate schemas in exec info and schema
 output

`info` and `schema <tool> <path>` printed the same sub-schema many
times per response and printed update tools in full right after their
create tool. On the friction session: DRF choice lists that repeat an
enum were 6,059 tokens; the two retention entity drills were 99.9%
identical; `info insight-update` (3,732 tokens) carried insight-create's
`query` schema again, and update-feature-flag and survey-update were 95%
their create tool.

What `info` and `schema <tool> <path>` print now goes through
compactSchema in schema-utils:

- A DRF choice line (`* \`once\` - once`) is dropped when its value is
  in the same node's enum and its label only repeats the value. A label
  that says more (`distinct_id` - "User ID (default)") stays. The
  summary view drops the same lines, since it keeps `enum`.
- A sub-schema that appears more than once in one response moves into
  `$defs` and each copy becomes a `$ref`. Copies may differ in
  description only, which then stays on the reference. Inlining the
  references again gives back the original schema (tested on
  query-retention).
- For an update tool whose create tool's `info` was printed in full
  earlier in the session, each top-level property identical in both is
  replaced by `{"$ref": "<create>#/properties/<name>"}` with a sentence
  saying where it was shown and how to see it again. Without that
  earlier `info`, or without a session, every property is printed.
  `info` records `shown:info:<tool>` in the session store when it
  prints a whole schema.

Whether `info` prints the whole schema or the summary is still decided
on the uncompacted size, so no tool switches from a summary to a larger
full schema. The exec change is limited to calling these functions in
the info and schema cases.

